# plymouth.manifest — system config owned by mod_plymouth (boot splash theme).
# Managed system paths (root to reset), restored from the W source. The swatch
# PNGs are w-style output (900-plymouth) painted from the SYSTEM theme — class
# `rendered`: their `w`-coloured seeds must not be copied over an existing render
# (the next initramfs build would bake them into the splash). `w-style apply all|plymouth`.
# Format: <path>\t<class>   (trailing '/' = directory)
/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/	managed
/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/bar.png	rendered
/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/bar-bg.png	rendered
/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/bullet.png	rendered
/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/lock.png	rendered
/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/pin.png	rendered
/etc/plymouth/plymouthd.conf	managed
/etc/systemd/system/plymouth-quit.service.d/override.conf	managed
